You are a formal verification assistant. The following Dafny program fails Dafny verification.

=== PROGRAM ===
method findMax(a:array<int>) returns (pos:int, maxVal: int)
  requires a.Length > 0;
  requires forall i :: 0 <= i < a.Length ==> a[i] >= 0;
  ensures forall i :: 0 <= i < a.Length ==> a[i] <= maxVal;
  ensures exists i :: 0 <= i < a.Length &&  a[i] == maxVal;
  ensures 0 <= pos < a.Length
  ensures a[pos] == maxVal;
{
  pos := 0;
  maxVal := a[0];
  var j := 1;
  while(j < a.Length)
    invariant 1 <= j <= a.Length;
    invariant forall i :: 0 <= i < j ==> a[i] <= maxVal;
    invariant exists i :: 0 <= i < j && a[i] == maxVal;
    invariant a[pos] == maxVal;
  {
    if (a[j] > maxVal) 
    {
      maxVal := a[j];
      pos := j;
    }
    j := j+1;
  }
  return;
}

=== DAFNY ERROR ===
program.dfy(16,15): Error: index out of range

program.dfy(25,2): Error: a postcondition could not be proved on this return path

program.dfy(6,19): Related location: this is the postcondition that could not be proved
  |
6 |   ensures 0 <= pos < a.Length
  |                    ^

Dafny program verifier finished with 1 verified, 2 errors

=== COUNTEREXAMPLE ===
For the error at line 16: At initial state: a.Length = 2283, a[0] = 609, a[2282] = 609. At a program state: pos = 0. At a program state: maxVal = 609. At a program state: j = 1.
For the error at line 25: At initial state: a.Length = 2283, a[0] = 2997, a[10648] = 2997, a[1140] = 2997, a[1] = 2997, a[8136] = 2998. At a program state: pos = 0. At a program state: maxVal = 2997. At a program state: j = 1.

Analyze the failure and respond with ONLY a valid JSON object — no explanation, no markdown, no code fences. Use exactly this structure:

{
  "spec_element": "<one of: requires | invariant | ensures>",
  "proof_obligation": "<one of: initiation | preservation | bridge>",
  "diagnosis": "<explanation of what broke and why>",
  "repair": "<the corrected Dafny specification line that restores the intended behavior>"
}

Definitions:
- requires: the precondition that must hold before the method executes
- invariant: the loop invariant that must hold throughout the loop
- ensures: the postcondition that the method must guarantee on return
- initiation: the precondition does not establish the invariant at loop entry
- preservation: the loop body does not maintain the invariant
- bridge: the invariant and loop exit condition do not imply the postcondition

